    description: "SOURCE: Process health synthesis 5.1, recommendation 10. The bakeoff operates in two phases: Phase 1 (intensive iteration on fixed repos, validating fixes as they land) and Phase 2 (validation sweep on new repos to confirm accumulated fixes generalize). This is effective but not formally documented — it was reconstructed from notebook entries and commit histories during the process health investigation. Adding a bakeoff strategy section to session metadata or a curriculum file (as described in ADR-0009 section 2b) would make the strategy legible to future agents and auditors. Should also document the expected Phase 3: deep-dive on Phase 2 repos that received WARN/PARTIALLY_USEFUL, which has not yet been done for cohorts 14-18."  # 2f13
